# Grip events (CCE 06035750, DUSA 0602C8E2). Code constants: all cars.
# Per-tick multiplier m converts to m^(2/3); tick counts convert x3/2
# (CCE already converted the 20-tick timer to 30).
DAYTONA/RACE.BIN 060358FC 06028000 000107ae 000110cb   # rear grip recovery x1.03 -> x1.0656 (DUSA x1.10 @20 Hz)
DAYTONA/RACE.BIN 06035796 06028000 e30a e30f           # event timer 10 -> 15 ticks
DAYTONA/RACE.BIN 060357B2 06028000 e210 e218           # shift-grip timer 16 -> 24 ticks
# Grass climb (060357B6, DUSA 0602C946): the 30-tick event starts when the
# pitch (+0x0C, DUSA's way since patch 21, same angle units) is over DUSA's
# 0x500, a wheel on grass and leaning against the slope; CCE had 0x600.
DAYTONA/RACE.BIN 06035862 06028000 0600 0500           # grass-climb pitch 0x600 -> 0x500
# Not ported, on purpose (the user, 2026-11-14): the first event's steering
# test. Over 70 km/h with the front and rear lateral forces of opposite sign,
# CCE starts the timer when the front wheel (+0xAC) is past 0x1000 either way
# (06035784-06035792). DUSA (0602C914-0602C922) starts it unless the wheel
# is at -0x1000 or below: lopsided, one steering side only, which reads as a
# flipped comparison in DUSA's source that CCE corrected. Kept symmetric.
